course: dictionary
lesson: 433
title: One word, many meanings: arc
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An arc is part of a curved line, such as part of a circle. Picture the bend of a rainbow, or a piece cut from the edge of a round plate. When you draw with a compass and make just a bend rather than a whole circle, you are drawing an arc.
explain: «The ball arced through the air.» Here arc is a verb, so it describes an action: the ball moved in a smooth curve, not in a straight line. The words «through the air» are the clue that the path went up and over.
explain: Stories can have arcs too. A story arc is the shape a story or a character follows from beginning to end. If a shy boy starts the book timid and finishes it brave, his character arc is the change he makes along the way.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to use. «The Alps arc across eight countries» describes a long chain of mountains bending across a map. «A shot from beyond the arc scores 3» is about the curved line marked on a basketball court. Always check the words around the word first.
fact: An arc is part of a curved line, such as part of a circle.
fact: Arc can be a noun («an arc») or a verb («to arc», «the ball arced»).
fact: A story arc is the shape of events or of a character's change from beginning to end.
fact: In science, an electric arc is a bright spark that jumps across a gap.
fact: Joan of Arc is a name with a capital letter; it is a person's name, not a different meaning of the word.
exercise: Which word means a curved part of a circle? | chord | diameter | *arc | radius
exercise: «The ball arced through the air.» What does arced mean here? | *Moved in a smooth curve through the air | Fell straight down into a box | Moved in a curve | Stopped dead on the ground
exercise: «The Alps arc across eight countries.» What does arc suggest here? | They are all in one small town | They are hidden under the sea | They are very small | *They bend in a long curve across the map
test: «In basketball a shot from beyond the arc scores 3.» What is the arc in this sentence? | The player's jump | A kind of basket | *The curved line marked on the court | A referee's whistle
test: What is a story arc? | A short poem | *The shape of change from beginning to end | A type of rainbow | Only the last page of a book
exam: In science, what is the bright spark that jumps across a gap called? | a rainbow | a shadow | a magnet | *an electric arc
